INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(27,'Category Guide – Crypto Casinos','cat-guide-crypto-casinos','text','What to Check Before Choosing a Crypto Casino','<p>Crypto casinos differ from standard operators in a few practical ways worth understanding before you fund an account. BC.GAME and Stake, for example, run their own in-house tokens (BCD and Stake Originals respectively) alongside standard coins like Bitcoin, Ethereum, Litecoin and USDT — these unlock loyalty perks and faster wagering but are not the same as your deposited crypto balance, so read how each platform separates the two.</p><p>Provably fair gaming is the other big differentiator. On games like Dice, Plinko and Limbo, the casino publishes a cryptographic seed you can use to independently verify that a result was not altered after you placed your bet. This does not apply to licensed slots from third-party studios, which are certified through the studio and regulator instead — check which category a game falls into before assuming it is provably fair.</p><p>Withdrawal speed is usually the strongest argument for playing crypto-first: Stake and Shuffle both process crypto cashouts in minutes once verification is complete, versus the multi-day waits common with card withdrawals elsewhere. That speed depends on your account being fully verified first, so complete KYC early rather than waiting until your first withdrawal.</p><p>Finally, confirm which coins a casino actually supports before depositing — Shuffle, for instance, lists Bitcoin, Ethereum, Litecoin, USDT, TRX, Matic and its own SHFL token, while BC.GAME supports a much wider spread including Dogecoin, Solana and BNB. Sending an unsupported coin to a deposit address can result in a permanently lost transaction.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(28,'Category Guide – Live Dealer Casinos','cat-guide-live-dealer-casinos','text','How to Evaluate a Live Dealer Casino','<p>A live dealer casino streams a real dealer running blackjack, roulette, baccarat or a game show from a studio, with your bets placed through the same interface as an RNG slot. The quality gap between operators comes down to a few concrete things: table variety, minimum and maximum bet limits, and how many tables run in your local peak hours versus off-hours.</p><p>Table limits matter more than most players expect. A casino advertising "live blackjack" might only run one or two tables at low stakes during quiet periods, while a larger operator with multiple studio partners keeps a full spread of VIP and standard tables live around the clock. If you play at a specific time of day, check table availability at that time before assuming the lobby you see on the homepage reflects what is actually open.</p><p>Latency and stream quality also vary by studio provider and your own connection, so a mobile-optimized live lobby is worth checking specifically if you plan to play on a phone rather than desktop — some casinos compress live streams more aggressively for mobile data, which affects the experience during fast-paced games like Crazy Time or Lightning Roulette.</p><p>Finally, live dealer games are rarely included in welcome bonus wagering requirements, or count at a reduced percentage (often 10-20%) even when they are. If a promotion looks aimed at live casino play, confirm the game-weighting table in the bonus terms before assuming your live blackjack sessions will clear it at the advertised rate.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(29,'Category Guide – Sportsbook Casinos','cat-guide-sportsbook-casinos','text','Playing Casino and Sports Betting on the Same Account','<p>Platforms like 1Win, Jet Casino and Neospin run a full casino and a full sportsbook under one login and, in most cases, one wallet balance. The convenience is real — you can cash out a casino win and stake it on a football match without moving funds between separate accounts — but it also means casino and sports bonuses are usually kept strictly separate, with their own wagering rules and eligible-game lists.</p><p>Coverage depth is the main thing to compare between operators. 1Win lists football, basketball, tennis, cricket, esports, MMA, boxing and horse racing with both pre-match and live markets; Jet Casino covers a similar spread with live betting on in-progress matches. If you follow a specific sport or league closely, check market depth for that sport specifically rather than assuming broad category coverage means deep odds on niche competitions.</p><p>Live streaming, where offered, is usually restricted to selected high-profile fixtures rather than every listed match, and often requires an active bet or minimum balance to unlock. If live streaming is a deciding factor for you, verify the eligibility rule before counting on it.</p><p>As with casino bonuses, sportsbook promotions such as accumulator boosts or cashback on losing bets carry their own terms — minimum odds, minimum leg count, and settlement timing all vary by operator, so read the specific promotion page rather than assuming standard sportsbook conventions apply everywhere.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(30,'Category Guide – Slot-Focused Casinos','cat-guide-slots-casinos','text','Choosing a Casino for Slot Variety','<p>Slot library size is the easiest number to compare between casinos, but it is a weak signal on its own — what matters more is which studios are behind the games. Fresh Casino, for example, works with Pragmatic Play, Evolution, NetEnt, Playtech, Play''n GO, BGaming, Wazdan, Amatic and Nolimit City, giving it both mainstream hits and higher-volatility niche titles from smaller studios that some larger casinos skip entirely.</p><p>Progressive jackpot slots pool a portion of every wager across a network of casinos, which is why the same jackpot title can show a different prize total on different sites — check the live jackpot value on the casino itself rather than a marketing page, since it changes constantly. Fixed-jackpot and "Hold & Win" style slots, by contrast, pay a set maximum regardless of network size, which some players find more predictable.</p><p>Volatility is worth understanding before you pick a session budget: low-volatility slots pay smaller wins more often and suit a longer session on a fixed budget, while high-volatility titles (common in Megaways and bonus-buy formats) can go long stretches without a payout before a larger hit. Most casinos list volatility in the game info panel — it is worth checking before you commit a bankroll to an unfamiliar title.</p><p>Finally, slot RTP (return to player) is set by the game studio, not the casino, so the same slot pays out at the same long-run rate wherever you play it. What does vary by casino is whether a promotion''s wagering requirement fully counts slots at 100% — some casinos weight certain high-RTP or bonus-buy slots lower specifically to prevent bonus abuse, so check the excluded-games list in the bonus terms.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(31,'Category Guide – New Casinos','cat-guide-new-casinos','text','What We Check Before Listing a New Casino','<p>A new casino goes through the same checklist we apply to established brands before it appears on this site — we do not relax our standards for newer platforms, and a handful of new casinos we have evaluated have not made the published list because they did not pass licensing or payment verification.</p><p>The first check is licensing: we confirm the operator holds an active gambling licence (commonly Curacao or Malta Gaming Authority for the casinos we cover) and that the licence number resolves to the correct operating entity, not a shell company reusing an old registration.</p><p>The second check is a real-money test of deposits and withdrawals, including how the casino handles identity verification (KYC) at withdrawal time. New casinos sometimes advertise fast payouts but only after an unadvertised, lengthy first-withdrawal verification process — we flag this explicitly when we see it rather than only reporting the advertised processing time.</p><p>Because a new casino has a shorter track record, we also monitor it more closely after listing than we do an established brand — watching for changes to ownership, licence status, or bonus terms in the weeks after launch, and updating or removing the listing if standards slip.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(32,'Country Guide – Canada','country-guide-ca','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Canada','<p>Gambling regulation in Canada is set at the provincial level rather than nationally. Ontario runs its own regulated online gambling market through AGCO/iGO, where operators must hold a provincial licence to legally offer real-money casino games to Ontario residents. Outside Ontario, most provinces do not license private online casinos directly, and Canadian players commonly use offshore-licensed sites instead — the legal position for players in those provinces is less clearly defined than in Ontario, so this is worth checking against your own province''s current rules rather than assuming the same position applies nationwide.</p><p>On the banking side, Canadian players typically look for CAD-denominated accounts (so you are not absorbing a currency conversion fee on every deposit) and familiar payment rails such as Interac e-Transfer, Visa, Mastercard and major e-wallets, alongside crypto options on platforms like Stake and BC.GAME. Processing times for Interac deposits are usually near-instant, while withdrawals back to a Canadian bank account can take longer depending on the casino''s verification process.</p><p>Whichever casino you choose, confirm it explicitly lists Canada — or your specific province — as a supported region before depositing, since access rules can differ from one operator to the next.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(33,'Country Guide – Australia','country-guide-au','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Australia','<p>Australia''s Interactive Gambling Act restricts the provision of online casino games to operators licensed within Australia, and no domestic licences are currently issued for online casino-style games — only wagering and lottery products are licensed domestically. In practice, Australian players who play online casino games are almost always doing so on offshore-licensed platforms (commonly Curacao or Malta-licensed), which operate outside Australian regulatory oversight rather than in violation of a specific player-facing prohibition. Because this area has real legal nuance and the rules are enforced primarily against operators rather than players, treat this section as background context, not legal advice, and check current guidance if you are uncertain.</p><p>Where offshore casinos do accept Australian players, most support AUD-denominated accounts to avoid conversion fees, along with Visa, Mastercard, POLi-style bank transfers, and crypto options such as Bitcoin and Ethereum on crypto-first platforms.</p><p>Because offshore operators can change their accepted-country list without much notice, always confirm current Australian availability directly on the casino before depositing rather than relying on an older listing.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(34,'Country Guide – New Zealand','country-guide-nz','text','Playing at Online Casinos From New Zealand','<p>New Zealand''s domestic licensing covers the TAB and Lotto NZ, along with a small number of licensed land-based casinos — it does not extend to online casino-style gambling. As with Australia, New Zealand players who play online casino games typically do so through offshore-licensed operators (often Curacao-licensed) rather than through a domestically licensed product. This is an area with genuine legal nuance rather than a simple yes/no, so treat this as background context and check current guidance if you are unsure of your position.</p><p>Offshore casinos that accept New Zealand players commonly support NZD-denominated accounts, Visa and Mastercard, and crypto payment rails on platforms like Stake and Shuffle. As with any offshore-facing market, accepted-country lists can change, so confirm current NZ availability directly on the casino before signing up.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(35,'Country Guide – Germany','country-guide-de','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Germany','<p>Germany regulates online gambling nationally under the Glucksspielstaatsvertrag (GlueStV), in force since mid-2021, through the joint gambling authority GGL. Under this framework, licensed operators can offer online slots and sports betting to German players, subject to strict rules including deposit limits, a slot-spin speed cap, and a cross-operator self-exclusion system (OASIS). Online table games and live dealer casino products sit outside most private operator licences under the current framework — access to those specific products from Germany is more restricted than slots or sports betting, so if live casino or table games are what you are looking for, check a given operator''s current licensed product list for Germany specifically rather than assuming full casino access is licensed.</p><p>Licensed operators must display their GGL licence information and enforce the platform-wide deposit limit (currently set per player across all licensed operators, not per casino) — a structural difference from most other markets covered on this site. Payment options on licensed sites typically include SEPA transfer, major cards, and Trustly-style instant bank payments.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(36,'Country Guide – Brazil','country-guide-br','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Brazil','<p>Brazil moved from an unregulated market to a federal licensing system under Law 14.790/2023, administered by the Secretaria de Premios e Apostas (SPA) within the Ministry of Finance. The regulated market became operational in January 2025, and by mid-2026 dozens of operators held active federal licences covering sports betting and online casino-style products, with unlicensed platforms facing domain blocking and payment blacklisting.</p><p>A key practical point for Brazilian players: only SPA-licensed operators are authorized to legally offer real-money online casino games in Brazil, and licensed platforms are required to process payments through Pix or another Central Bank-authorized rail rather than international cards or crypto. If a casino you are considering is not SPA-licensed, it is operating outside this framework — check for explicit Brazilian federal licensing on the operator''s site before assuming a global brand''s licence covers Brazil specifically.</p><p>Because this market changed substantially in 2025-2026 and enforcement has continued to tighten, treat licensing claims as something to verify directly on the SPA''s current operator registry rather than take on trust from a casino''s own marketing.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(37,'Country Guide – South Africa','country-guide-za','text','Playing at Online Casinos From South Africa','<p>South Africa''s National Gambling Act framework primarily covers licensed sports betting and land-based casinos; comprehensive national licensing for online casino-style games has not been broadly implemented, and most South African players accessing online casino games do so through offshore-licensed operators. This is a genuinely unsettled area of local regulation rather than a simple prohibition or permission, so treat this section as background rather than legal advice and check current guidance if you are unsure.</p><p>Where offshore casinos accept South African players, ZAR-denominated accounts, EFT bank transfers, and major cards are the most common payment options, with crypto available on platforms like Stake and BC.GAME. As with other offshore-facing markets, confirm current South African availability directly on the casino before depositing.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(38,'Country Guide – Finland','country-guide-fi','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Finland','<p>Finland is in the middle of ending Veikkaus'' decades-long gambling monopoly. A new Gambling Act was approved in January 2026, with licence applications for private B2C operators opening on 1 March 2026 — but Veikkaus retains its monopoly on online betting, slots and casino games until 30 June 2027, when the licensed multi-operator market is scheduled to formally open. As of 2026, most non-Veikkaus online casinos serving Finnish players are still operating without a Finnish licence, since none can be issued yet.</p><p>If you are reading this before the July 2027 market opening, treat any casino''s claim of "Finnish licensing" with scrutiny — no private operator licences exist yet, and this will be one of the fastest-moving regulatory situations covered on this site. Once licensed operators launch, check for a valid licence issued by Finland''s new Licensing and Supervisory Authority before assuming a casino is operating within the new framework.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
INSERT INTO "components" ("id","name","slug","type","title","content","settings_json","status","created_at","updated_at") VALUES(39,'Country Guide – Norway','country-guide-no','text','Playing at Online Casinos From Norway','<p>Norway maintains a state monopoly model, with Norsk Tipping and Norsk Rikstoto as the only domestically licensed gambling operators. Norway has also implemented payment-blocking measures aimed at preventing Norwegian banks from processing transactions to unlicensed foreign gambling operators, making deposits to offshore casinos less straightforward than in markets without such restrictions — some players route deposits through crypto or e-wallets specifically because direct card payments to offshore casinos are frequently blocked at the Norwegian bank level.</p><p>Because of this, if a casino lists NOK support or Norwegian-language pages, check whether card deposits actually process from a Norwegian bank before assuming full functionality — payment friction is the most common practical issue Norwegian players report with offshore-licensed casinos, more so than access to the site itself.</p>',NULL,'active','2026-08-27 22:20:33','2026-08-27 22:20:33');
